      "summary": "The child process handles parsing and supervision, but the Unix working-directory restriction can be bypassed when the API runs as root.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api/Evidence/IsolatedPdfParser.cs",
          "line": 148,
          "message": "The Unix permission change does not make the worker directory read-only when the API runs as root; use an access restriction the worker cannot bypass.",
          "confidence": 0.84,
          "category": "security A01:2025",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "On Linux, RestrictWorkingDirectory removes write bits with chmod, but the child keeps the API process identity and receives no separate user or capability restriction.",
            "failureScenario": "If the API runs as root, a crafted PDF exploits the worker, and the worker attempts to create a file in its working directory, root can bypass the directory's mode bits and write succeeds. The working directory is therefore not actually read-only in that deployment."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
